.TH XUR.STD.STUB.IL2CPP 7 "2026-10-30" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.stub.il2cpp \- interact with a live Unity Il2Cpp game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::stub::il2cpp;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::stub::il2cpp
provides runtime access to a Unity Il2Cpp game's types, fields,
methods, and objects from inside the injected process. It is the
primary module for writing game mods and trainers.
.PP
Fields can be read/written, methods can be invoked, and methods can
be hooked with closures that intercept calls at runtime.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B loaded() -> Result<Runtime>
Get the Il2Cpp runtime handle. Fails if Il2Cpp has not initialised yet.
.TP
.B null() -> Object
Return a null managed object reference.
.SH Runtime METHODS
.TP
.B class(assembly, namespace, name) -> Result<Class>
Look up a managed class by assembly name, namespace, and class name.
.TP
.B string(value) -> Object
Create a managed System.String from a xur string.
.TP
.B assemblies() -> [Image]
List all loaded assemblies as Image objects.
.SH Class METHODS
.TP
.B field(name) -> Result<Field>
Look up a field by name.
.TP
.B method(name, param_count) -> Result<Method>
Look up a method by name and parameter count.
.TP
.B new_object() -> Object
Allocate a new managed object of this class (does not call a constructor).
.TP
.B fields() -> [Field]
List all fields on the class.
.TP
.B methods() -> [Method]
List all methods on the class.
.TP
.B name() -> str
The class name.
.TP
.B namespace() -> str
The class namespace.
.SH Field METHODS
.TP
.B read(object) -> value
Read this instance field's value from an object. The return type depends
on the field's element type (bool, int, float, or Object).
.TP
.B write(object, value) -> ()
Write a value to this instance field on an object.
.TP
.B read_static() -> value
Read a static field's value.
.TP
.B write_static(value) -> ()
Write a value to a static field.
.TP
.B name() -> str
The field name.
.TP
.B type_name() -> str
The field's type name.
.TP
.B offset() -> int
The field's offset in the object layout.
.TP
.B is_static() -> bool
Whether the field is static.
.SH Method METHODS
.TP
.B invoke(object, args...) -> value
Call the method via il2cpp_runtime_invoke. The first argument after the
method is the instance object (or
.BR null() ).
Remaining arguments are boxed and passed to the method.
.TP
.B hook(callback) -> ()
Install a generic hook on this method. The callback receives a
.B HookContext
and returns
.B Option<value>
\(em
.B None
passes through to the original,
.B Some(value)
overrides the return value.
.TP
.B hook_void_block() -> VoidBlockHook
Install a simple block/unblock hook. When blocked, the method returns
immediately without executing. Useful for void methods where you just
want to prevent execution.
.TP
.B name() -> str
The method name.
.TP
.B signature() -> str
The full method signature string.
.TP
.B code_address() -> int
The native code address of the method.
.SH HookContext METHODS
Available inside a
.BR hook() " callback:"
.TP
.B arg(index_or_name) -> value
Read a marshalled argument by index (int) or parameter name (str).
.TP
.B args() -> [value]
All marshalled arguments as a list.
.TP
.B set_arg(index_or_name, value) -> ()
Mark an argument as modified. Changes are written back to the
saved registers before the original is called.
.TP
.B signature() -> str
The hooked method's signature string.
.TP
.B call() -> value
Call the original method with the (possibly modified) arguments.
Can only be called once per hook invocation. Returns the original's
return value.
.SH VoidBlockHook METHODS
.TP
.B set_blocked(blocked: bool) -> ()
Enable or disable blocking.
.TP
.B is_blocked() -> bool
Whether the hook is currently blocking.
.SH Image METHODS
.TP
.B name() -> str
The assembly image name.
.TP
.B classes() -> [Class]
All classes in this assembly image.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::stub::il2cpp;
use std::log;

fn ctor() {
    log::subscriber().to_file("/tmp/mod.log").init();
}

fn stub_main() {
    let rt = il2cpp::loaded().unwrap();
    let cls = rt.class("Assembly-CSharp", "", "PlayerHealth").unwrap();
    let hp = cls.field("hp").unwrap();
    let damage = cls.method("DamagePlayer", 3).unwrap();

    // Godmode: intercept damage calls
    damage.hook(|ctx| {
        log::info("blocked damage");
        Some(0)
    });
}
.fi
